          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The theorem of
            %a{:href => "#BenabouRoubaud70"} Bénabou &amp; Roubaud 1970
            identifies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras over
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            induced from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            satisfying the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+descent+data"} category of descent data
            along this morphism. This is the basis for the monadic reformulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            theory:
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
          %h2#context_2 Context
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \colon F\to A
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+opfibration"} Grothendieck opfibration
            if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+functor"} opposite functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^{op} \colon F^{op}\to A^{op}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            if it is both: a Grothendieck opfibration and fibration (no additional compatibility asked!). In this case we may speak about both
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocartesian+morphism"} cocartesian
            morphisms in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            Given a bifibration
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \colon F\to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A_1\to A_0
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"}> inverse image
            ” (or “pullback” or “restriction”) functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^*:F(A_0)\to F(A_1)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the “pushforward” functor
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo !
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_!:F(A_1)\to F(A_0)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} unit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Id
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta^a : Id_{F(A_1)} \to a^* a_!
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} counit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Id
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon^a : a_! a^* \to Id_{F(A_0)}
          %p
            (Note that in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^*
            called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+images"}> inverse images
            ” usually have
            %em right
            adjoints
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^*
            has both a left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_!
            %em and
            a right adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_*
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_!\dashv a^*
            generates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                    %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi μ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi η
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}^a=(T^a,\mu^a,\eta^a)
            in the usual way: the functor is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^a = a^* a_!\colon  F(A_1)\to F(A_1)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi μ
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi a
                      %mo *
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mo !
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu^a = a^* \epsilon^a a_!\colon  T^a \circ T^a \to T^a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^a
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg%E2%80%93Moore+category"} Eilenberg–Moore category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi T
                        %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A_1)^{\mathbf{T}^a}
            of modules (algebras) over the monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}^a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^{\mathbf{T}} \colon  F^a \to F(A_1)
            and canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+functor"} comparison functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^a \colon F(A_0) \to F^a
          %p
            Now we assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            satisfies what is nowadays called the
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+property"} Beck-Chevalley property
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %mi χ
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi k
                                  %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mi χ
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi M
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  N_0 &amp; \stackrel{\chi'}\leftarrow &amp; N_1
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{k_0}}\downarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{k_1}}
                  \\\
                  M_0 &amp;\stackrel{\chi}\leftarrow &amp; M_1
                  }
          %p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            such that its image in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            square, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi'
            are cartesian and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_0
            is cocartesian then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_1
            is cocartesian.
          %p An equivalent way to state the condition is that for any pullback square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi x
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi a
                        %mtd
                          %mi y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi b
                        %mtd
                          %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  x &amp; \overset{a}{\to} &amp; y
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{c}} \downarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{d}}
                  \\\
                  z &amp; \underset{b}{\to} &amp; w
                  }
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_! a^* \to b^* d_!
            is an isomorphism. In the Bénabou–Roubaud paper this is called the
            %em Chevalley property
            and said to make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            into a
            = succeed "." do
              %em Chevalley functor
          %p
            Denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2 :=A_1\times_{A_0}A_1
            the pullback of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            along itself, with the canonical projections
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1,a_2\colon A_2\to A_1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            in such a way that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_1
            is lifted to a cartesian arrow,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_2
            to a cocartesian arrow, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            to a cocartesian arrow. Then by the universality there is a lift of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            completing the square, and by the Beck–Chevalley property it is cartesian. Together with the isomorphism given by adjunction this gives a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msubsup
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K^a: Hom_{F(A_2)}(a_1^*(M_1),a_2^*(M_1))\to Hom_{F(A_1)}(T^a(M_1),M_1).
          %p
            One checks that an invertible morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon a_1^*(M_1)\to a_2^*(M_1)
            satisfies the cocycle equation (making it into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            datum) iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^a(\phi)
            is an action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}^a
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_1
          %h2#the_theorem The theorem
          %p
            Denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Desc(a)
            the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            data for the fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            along the morphism
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi^a\colon F(A_0)\to Desc(a)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U^a\colon Desc(a)\to F(A_1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The
            %strong Bénabou–Roubaud theorem
            asserts that this induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Desc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Desc(a)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^a
          %p
            In addition, this equivalence satisfies some naturality properties, including that it commutes appropriately with the canonical functors to the fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A_0)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(A_1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
          %p
            There are several characterizations of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+property"} Beck-Chevalley property
            for bifibrations:
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p (Duško Pavlović, in Category theory Como 1990, LNM 1488, Springer 1991)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi F
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: F\to B
              be a bifibration,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q = (f,g,s,t)
              a square in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\circ g = s\circ t
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta = (\phi, \gamma, \sigma, \theta)
              a square in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi γ
                      %mo =
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi θ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\circ\gamma=\sigma\circ\theta
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\phi)=f
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\gamma)=g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\sigma)=s
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi θ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi t
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\theta)=t
            %p
              a) if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              are cartesian and if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is cocartesian
              %em then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              must be cocartesian;
            %p
              b) if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              are cocartesian and if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              is cartesian
              %em then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              must be cartesian;
            %p
              c) if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
              is cartesian and if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is cocartesian
              %em then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is cartesian iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
              is cocartesian.
            %p
              If some inverse image functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t^*
              and some direct image functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_!
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_!
              are chosen, then every square
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              satisfies conditions (a-c) iff there is a canonical natural isomorphism
            %p
              d)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mo !
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi g
                        %mo !
                      %mo ∘
                      %msup
                        %mi t
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*\circ s_! \cong g_! \circ t^*
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beck-Chevalley+condition"} Beck-Chevalley condition
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#BenabouRoubaud70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Roubaud"} Jacques Roubaud
              = succeed "," do
                %em Monades et descente
              %strong 270
              (1970) 96-98 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k480298g/f100"}> gallica:12148/bpt6k480298g/f100
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BenabouRoubaud-MonadesEtDescente.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Heinig"} Peter Heinig
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/279152"} MO:q/279152
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#JanelidzeTholen94
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"}> George Janelidze
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Facets of Descent I
            %li#JanelidzeTholen97
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"}> George Janelidze
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Facets of Descent II
            %li
              %p
                X. Guo, thesis, p. 58 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monadicity, purity and descent equivalence
                %a{:href => "http://www.collectionscanada.gc.ca/obj/s4/f2/dsk2/ftp02/NQ59136.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            There has been some historical discussion on this in the category list; Zoran’s response is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathlight.wordpress.com/2010/01/07/becks-theorem-vs-benabou-roubaud"} here
          %p The following reference presents a proof for a (generalization) of the Bénabou-Roubaud Theorem (pages 435 and 436):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fernando+Lucatelli+Nunes"}> Fernando Lucatelli Nunes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Pseudo-Kan extensions and descent theory
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/33/15/33-15abs.html"} 33-15
